Chapter 5 — The Safety-Filter Quadratic Program

5.1 QP Formulation

Let $\mathbf{u}^{\rm AI}=k_{\rm nom}(\mathbf{x})$ be the nominal AI control. The Safety Kernel solves

\mathbf{u}^* = \arg\min_{\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{U}}\ \tfrac12\|\mathbf{u}-\mathbf{u}^{\rm AI}\|^2
\tag{5.1}

subject to the HOCBF constraints

L_f \psi_{r-1}^{(i)} + L_g \psi_{r-1}^{(i)}\mathbf{u} + \alpha_r^{(i)}(\psi_{r-1}^{(i)}) \ge \iota^{(i)}(\|\mathbf{d}\|),\quad \forall i,
\tag{5.2}

the friction envelope (3.12), the regenerative bound (3.16), and the box constraints

\mathbf{u}_{\min}\le \mathbf{u}\le \mathbf{u}_{\max},\qquad
\mathbf{u}_{\min}=[-a_{\rm dec,max},\ -\kappa_{\max}]^\top,\quad
\mathbf{u}_{\max}=[a_{\rm acc,max},\ \kappa_{\max}]^\top.
\tag{5.3}

In standard form with $\mathbf{z}=[a,\kappa]^\top$:

\min_{\mathbf{z}}\ \tfrac12\mathbf{z}^\top H\mathbf{z} + \mathbf{f}^\top\mathbf{z}
\quad\text{s.t.}\quad
A_{\rm cbf}\mathbf{z}\ge \mathbf{b}_{\rm cbf},\quad
\mathbf{z}_{\min}\le\mathbf{z}\le\mathbf{z}_{\max},
\tag{5.4}

with $H=2I_2$, $\mathbf{f}=-2\mathbf{u}^{\rm AI}$. The QP has $m=2$ decision variables and $N_{\rm cbf}+2m$ constraints, and is strongly convex; hence it admits a unique minimizer whenever feasible.

5.2 Sign Convention

Throughout this thesis, $a$ denotes signed longitudinal acceleration in $\mathrm{m/s^2}$: $a>0$ accelerates, $a<0$ decelerates. Emergency braking corresponds to

\mathbf{u}_{\rm backup}=(-a_{\rm dec,max},\,0),
\tag{5.5}

and the stopping-distance condition is

\frac{v^2}{2a_{\rm dec,max}}<d_{\rm safe}.
\tag{5.6}

5.3 Fixed-Iteration Active-Set Solver with WCET Bound

To meet ASIL-D timing requirements, we employ a fixed-iteration, warm-started active-set solver with the following properties:

· The active set is warm-started from the previous cycle, so the number of iterations per cycle is bounded by a small constant $N_{\rm it}$ (empirically $\le 3$ for the scenarios of Chapter 10).
· Floating-point operations per iteration are bounded; the WCET is therefore

T_{\rm WCET} \le N_{\rm it}\cdot T_{\rm iter} + T_{\rm setup},
\tag{5.7}

with $T_{\rm iter}\le 6\,\mu\mathrm{s}$ and $T_{\rm setup}\le 2\,\mu\mathrm{s}$ on the AURIX TC3xx at 300 MHz, yielding $T_{\rm WCET}\le 20\,\mu\mathrm{s}$.

· Numerical certificates (KKT residuals, dual feasibility) are computed and logged; if the certificate fails, the safety island transitions to the fallback within one control cycle.

