Chapter 7 — Universal Vehicle Abstraction Layer

7.1 Design Principles

1. Minimality. UVAL exposes only motion primitives.
2. Semantic level. Commands are physical quantities, not actuator signals.
3. Safety-first. Every primitive has explicit pre- and postconditions.
4. Manufacturer independence. The API never references a specific vehicle.
5. Real-time. All primitives execute at 100 Hz.

7.2 Formal Interface Specification

Let the vehicle state be

\mathrm{state} = (v,\delta,\mathrm{SOC},\mathrm{mode}),
\tag{7.1}

where $v$ is speed, $\delta$ is steering angle, $\mathrm{SOC}$ is battery state of charge, and $\mathrm{mode}\in\{\mathrm{manual},\mathrm{autonomous},\mathrm{emergency}\}$. Let the command be

\mathrm{command} = (\tau,a,\kappa,\mathrm{id}),
\tag{7.2}

where $\tau$ is torque, $a$ is signed acceleration in $\mathrm{m/s^2}$, $\kappa$ is curvature, and $\mathrm{id}$ is a command identifier.

Convention. $a<0$ decelerates; $a>0$ accelerates. Emergency braking is $a=-a_{\rm dec,max}$.

TorqueRequest$(\tau)$.
Precondition:
\mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous},\quad \mathrm{SOC}>5\%,\quad |\tau|\le \tau_{\max}.
\tag{7.3}


Postcondition:
\mathrm{command}' = (\tau,0,0,\mathrm{new\_id}).
\tag{7.4}

DecelRequest$(a)$.
Precondition:
\mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous},\quad -a_{\rm dec,max}\le a\le 0.
\tag{7.5}


Postcondition:
\mathrm{command}' = (0,a,0,\mathrm{new\_id}).
\tag{7.6}

CurvatureRequest$(\kappa)$.
Precondition:
\mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous},\quad |\kappa|\le \kappa_{\max}.
\tag{7.7}


Postcondition:
\mathrm{command}' = (0,0,\kappa,\mathrm{new\_id}).
\tag{7.8}

EnergyRequest$(\mathrm{SOC}_{\rm target})$.
Precondition:
\mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous},\quad \mathrm{SOC}\ge \mathrm{SOC}_{\min},\quad \mathrm{SOC}_{\rm target}\ge \mathrm{SOC}_{\min}.
\tag{7.9}


Postcondition: the adapter schedules charging or energy-saving actions subject to $h_{\rm SOC}\ge 0$.

RegenLimit$(P_{\rm regen})$.
Precondition:
0\le P_{\rm regen}\le P_{\rm regen,max},\quad \mathrm{SOC}<100\%.
\tag{7.10}


Postcondition: regenerative braking authority is set to $P_{\rm regen}$, and the input bound (3.16) is updated.

SafetyOverride.
Precondition: $\mathrm{true}$.
Postcondition:
\mathrm{mode}' = \mathrm{emergency},\quad
\mathrm{command}' = (0,-a_{\rm dec,max},0,\mathrm{emergency\_id}).
\tag{7.11}

Error semantics. If any precondition fails, the primitive is a no-op:
\text{Precondition false}\implies \mathrm{command}'=\mathrm{command},\quad \mathrm{error}'=\mathrm{true}.
\tag{7.12}

7.3 Adapter Contract

Calibrate.
Precondition: $\mathrm{adapter\_state}=\mathrm{uninitialized}$.
Postcondition: $\mathrm{adapter\_state}=\mathrm{calibrated}$.

TranslateTorque$(\tau)$.
Precondition: $\mathrm{adapter\_state}=\mathrm{calibrated}$.
Postcondition: a CAN frame with identifier 0x123 and payload $\mathrm{TorqueToCAN}(\tau)$ is appended to the bus.

EmergencyStop.
Precondition: $\mathrm{true}$.
Postcondition: $\mathrm{adapter\_state}=\mathrm{emergency}$, and a CAN frame with identifier 0x001 and payload {0xFF,0xFF,0xFF,0xFF} is appended.

GetCapabilities.
Precondition: $\mathrm{adapter\_state}=\mathrm{calibrated}$.
Postcondition: returns $(\tau_{\max},a_{\rm dec,max},a_{\rm acc,max},\kappa_{\max},\mathrm{supports\_curvature},\mathrm{regen\_capability})$.

DiagnosticCheck.
Precondition: $\mathrm{adapter\_state}\in\{\mathrm{calibrated},\mathrm{emergency}\}$.
Postcondition: returns $(\mathrm{relay\_state}_1,\mathrm{relay\_state}_2,\mathrm{welded\_contact\_detected})$.

