F.2.1 TorqueRequest

Signature. TorqueRequest(τ: ℝ) → (command', error')

Precondition.
P_{\rm torque}:\quad \mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous}\ \wedge\ \mathrm{SOC}>5\%\ \wedge\ |\tau|\le\tau_{\max}.

Postcondition.
Q_{\rm torque}:\quad P_{\rm torque}\implies \mathrm{command}'=(\tau,0,0,\mathrm{new\_id})\ \wedge\ \mathrm{error}'=\mathrm{false}.


Q_{\rm torque}^{\rm err}:\quad \neg P_{\rm torque}\implies \mathrm{command}'=\mathrm{command}\ \wedge\ \mathrm{error}'=(\mathrm{true},\mathrm{E\_TORQUE\_PRECOND}).

F.2.2 DecelRequest

Signature. DecelRequest(a: ℝ) → (command', error')

Precondition.
P_{\rm decel}:\quad \mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous}\ \wedge\ -a_{\rm dec,max}\le a\le 0.

Postcondition.
Q_{\rm decel}:\quad P_{\rm decel}\implies \mathrm{command}'=(0,a,0,\mathrm{new\_id}).

F.2.3 CurvatureRequest

Signature. CurvatureRequest(κ: ℝ) → (command', error')

Precondition.
P_{\rm curv}:\quad \mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous}\ \wedge\ |\kappa|\le\kappa_{\max}.

Postcondition.
Q_{\rm curv}:\quad P_{\rm curv}\implies \mathrm{command}'=(0,0,\kappa,\mathrm{new\_id}).

F.2.4 EnergyRequest

Signature. EnergyRequest(SOC_target: ℝ) → (command', error')

Precondition.
P_{\rm energy}:\quad \mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{autonomous}\ \wedge\ \mathrm{SOC}\ge\mathrm{SOC}_{\min}\ \wedge\ \mathrm{SOC}_{\rm target}\ge\mathrm{SOC}_{\min}.

Postcondition. The adapter schedules charging or energy-saving actions subject to $h_{\rm SOC}\ge 0$.

F.2.5 RegenLimit

Signature. RegenLimit(P_regen: ℝ) → (command', error')

Precondition.
P_{\rm regen}:\quad 0\le P_{\rm regen}\le P_{\rm regen,max}\ \wedge\ \mathrm{SOC}<100\%.

Postcondition. Regenerative braking authority is set to $P_{\rm regen}$, and the input bound (3.16) is updated.

F.2.6 SafetyOverride

Signature. SafetyOverride() → (mode', command', error')

Precondition.
P_{\rm override}:\quad \mathrm{true}.

Postcondition.
Q_{\rm override}:\quad \mathrm{mode}'=\mathrm{emergency}\ \wedge\ \mathrm{command}'=(0,-a_{\rm dec,max},0,\mathrm{emergency\_id}).

F.2.7 DiagnosticCheck

Signature. DiagnosticCheck() → (relay₁, relay₂, welded)

Precondition.
P_{\rm diag}:\quad \mathrm{adapter\_state}\in\{\mathrm{calibrated},\mathrm{emergency}\}.

Postcondition. Returns $(\mathrm{relay\_state}_1,\mathrm{relay\_state}_2,\mathrm{welded\_contact\_detected})$.

F.3 Invariants

Invariant F.1 (Mode consistency). At all times, $\mathrm{mode}\in\{\mathrm{manual},\mathrm{autonomous},\mathrm{emergency}\}$.

Invariant F.2 (Command freshness). Every command carries a strictly increasing $\mathrm{id}$.

Invariant F.3 (Emergency dominance). Once $\mathrm{mode}=\mathrm{emergency}$, no primitive except SafetyOverride may change the command.

Invariant F.4 (Energy floor). The EnergyRequest and RegenLimit primitives maintain $h_{\rm SOC}\ge 0$.

