Appendix I — Experimental Protocol

I.1 Scenario Definitions

S1: Straight Line. The vehicle follows a straight path of length 10 m at constant speed. Metrics: RMS tracking error $e_{\rm rms}$, control loop latency $t_{\rm loop}$.

S2: Curved Path. The vehicle follows a sinusoidal path of length 20 m. Metrics: lateral error $e_{\max}$, curvature tracking error.

S3: Static Obstacle Avoidance. A static obstacle is placed on the path. Metrics: minimum distance $d_{\min}$, safety intervention rate $\rho_{\rm int}$.

S4: Dynamic Obstacle Avoidance. A moving obstacle crosses the path with acceleration up to $\bar a_o$. Metrics: HOCBF feasibility, $d_{\rm inf}$, fallback rate $\rho_{\rm fallback}$.

S5: Emergency Stop. The vehicle performs an emergency stop from $v_{\max}$. Metrics: stopping distance $d_{\rm stop}$, deceleration profile.

S6: CAN Latency Injection. Artificial latency up to $\bar d$ is injected. Metrics: robust feasibility rate $\rho_{\rm feas}$.

S7: Adversarial Obstacle Acceleration. The obstacle accelerates up to $\bar a_o$. Metrics: minimum distance $d_{\min}$, certificate validity.

S8: EV Energy Depletion. The vehicle operates until SOC approaches $\mathrm{SOC}_{\min}$. Metrics: SOC trajectory, $h_{\rm SOC}$ margin.

S9: Sensor Noise Injection. Gaussian noise is added to position and velocity. Metrics: tracking error, QP feasibility.

I.2 Data Logging

All scenarios log at 1 kHz:

· State $\mathbf{x}_k$.
· AI command $\mathbf{u}^{\rm AI}_k$.
· Safety-filter output $\mathbf{u}^\star_k$.
· KKT residual and certificate status.
· Constraint slacks $\psi_i(\mathbf{x}_k)-\varepsilon_i$.
· Distance-to-infeasibility $d_{\rm inf}(\mathbf{x}_k)$.

I.3 Statistical Analysis

For each metric, report mean, standard deviation, and 95% confidence interval over $N\ge 30$ runs. Use a one-sided $t$-test to verify that $d_{\rm inf}>0$ with confidence 99%.

I.4 Falsifiability Conditions

The thesis is falsified if any of the following occurs:

1. HOCBF-QP infeasibility occurs for $>10\%$ of control cycles in nominal scenarios.
2. $t_{\rm QP}>100\,\mu$s or $t_{\rm loop}>20$ ms.
3. Any collision or loss of control occurs in S1–S9.
4. The Dacia Spring cannot be controlled via CAN retrofit.
5. The Moroccan Ministry of Transport rejects the retrofit.
6. The architecture cannot be ported to a second vehicle within three months.
7. $d_{\rm inf}$ becomes nonpositive in nominal scenarios.
8. $h_{\rm SOC}$ becomes negative under normal operation.

